 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "bosch 24 not draining, water sitting in bottom. help"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "I can help. Water left in the bottom usually means a drain blockage, filter/pump issue or drain-hose problem, but the checks differ by appliance. Is it a Bosch dishwasher, washing machine or tumble dryer? “24” is likely a model/series reference rather than enough to identify it."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "dishwasher. Bosch, display shows E:24. model SMS24AW01G"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "E:24 on this Bosch indicates it cannot drain, most commonly from a blocked filter/sump, debris at the drain pump, or a kinked/blocked drain hose or sink-waste connection. Start with the filter: switch it off and unplug it, remove the lower rack, twist out the filter in the base and rinse it clean. Use a cup and sponge to remove enough standing water to look into the sump underneath; use a torch and remove any loose food, labels or visible glass (wear gloves for glass). If the filter and sump are clear, the next likely causes are something caught in the pump or a hose/waste blockage.\n[Helpful to see: image \"Where the filter is\" — The filter sits in the base of the dishwasher, usually under the bottom spray arm. Twist it out anticlockwise and rinse it under a tap. Typical layout — your dishwasher may differ.]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "filter was clogged with food and a bit of broken glass. cleaned it, now drains ok and E:24 has gone"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Check and rinse the filter regularly, and take care with broken glass as small pieces can reach the pump area. If E:24 returns despite a clean filter, the next suspects would be debris at the pump or a restriction in the drain hose/waste connection."
  }
 ],
